                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_08\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes the declaration of HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME in TetrisPanel.java from\n`private static final int HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";` to\n`private static final String HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";`, i.e. it corrects\na type mismatch (a String literal was incorrectly declared with type `int`), which is a\ncompile-time error (\"fix build error\").\n\ncandidate_08 is the commit that first introduces this exact line:\n`private static final int HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";`\nas part of a larger refactor that converts several instance fields (WIDTH, HEIGHT, ROWS,\nCOLUMNS, INIT_DELAY, etc.) into `static final` constants, and adds new constants including\nHIGH_SCORES_FILENAME, MAX_HIGH_SCORES, SCORE_INCREMENT_VALUE, and TEXT_COLOR. In this same\ncommit, the previously hardcoded string literal \"TetrisHighScores.txt\" (used directly in\n`new File(...)` and `new FileWriter(...)` calls) was replaced by the new HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME\nconstant \u2014 but the constant was mistakenly declared as `int` instead of `String`, introducing\nthe build-breaking bug that the fix commit later resolves.\n\nNo earlier candidate contains this field at all (it did not exist prior to candidate_08), and\ncandidate_09 already reflects the corrected `String` type, matching the fix commit's diff\nexactly. Therefore candidate_08 is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
